review_comments.body:
_⚠️ Potential issue_

**Mismatch between Rust FFI and dummy implementation – add `cudaStream_t`**

The Rust side passes an extra `CUstream` argument.  These dummy functions are missing it, so the call stack will be corrupted if they are ever invoked (e.g. on CC < 8.0 GPUs).

Apply for all three stubs:

```diff
-    int weight_row_stride, int scale_stride, int block_y, int block_x) {
+    int weight_row_stride, int scale_stride, int block_y, int block_x,
+    cudaStream_t /*stream*/) {
```

(and mark the parameter as unused to silence warnings).


```diff
@@
-    int weight_row_stride, int scale_stride, int block_y, int block_x) {
+    int weight_row_stride, int scale_stride, int block_y, int block_x,
+    cudaStream_t /*stream*/) {
@@
-    int weight_row_stride, int scale_stride, int block_y, int block_x) {
+    int weight_row_stride, int scale_stride, int block_y, int block_x,
+    cudaStream_t /*stream*/) {
@@
-    int weight_row_stride, int scale_stride, int block_y, int block_x) {
+    int weight_row_stride, int scale_stride, int block_y, int block_x,
+    cudaStream_t /*stream*/) {
```


<!-- suggestion_start -->

<details>
<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>

> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**
> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.

```suggestion
extern "C" void launch_gemm_fp8_blockwise_kernel_f16(
    const uint8_t* weight, const float* scale, const uint16_t* input,
    uint16_t* output, int batch, int in_dim, int out_dim,
    int weight_row_stride, int scale_stride, int block_y, int block_x,
    cudaStream_t /*stream*/) {
  assert(false);
}

extern "C" void launch_gemm_fp8_blockwise_kernel_bf16(
    const uint8_t* weight, const float* scale, const uint16_t* input,
    uint16_t* output, int batch, int in_dim, int out_dim,
    int weight_row_stride, int scale_stride, int block_y, int block_x,
    cudaStream_t /*stream*/) {
  assert(false);
}

extern "C" void launch_gemm_fp8_blockwise_kernel_f32(
    const uint8_t* weight, const float* scale, const float* input,
    float* output, int batch, int in_dim, int out_dim,
    int weight_row_stride, int scale_stride, int block_y, int block_x,
    cudaStream_t /*stream*/) {
  assert(false);
}
```

</details>

<!-- suggestion_end -->

<details>
<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>

```
In mistralrs-quant/kernels/blockwise_fp8/blockwise_fp8_gemm_dummy.cu lines 5 to
24, the three dummy kernel launch functions lack the cudaStream_t parameter
present in the Rust FFI, causing a mismatch and potential call stack corruption.
Add a cudaStream_t parameter to each function signature, mark it as unused to
avoid warnings, and keep the assert(false) inside the function body unchanged.
```

</details>

